# How docky is installed. One non-comment line; read by scripts/70-docker.sh and
# by the CI `tools` job, so CI always tests the spec the substrate installs.
#
# The PyPI release's setup.cfg carries a [bdist_wheel] python-tag section, so the
# sdist builds a wheel with the invalid tag `py34+`: old pip only warned, pip 26.x
# (the one pipx puts in its shared venv) hard-fails with "Built wheel for docky is
# invalid: Invalid wheel filename (invalid tag component)" and takes the whole
# install down. akretion/docky branch fix-py3-wheel-tag drops that section.
#
# Override at run time with DOCKY_SPEC=<spec> (e.g. DOCKY_SPEC=docky once a fixed
# release is on PyPI). Pin the commit for a frozen install:
#   git+https://github.com/akretion/docky@714eb68
git+https://github.com/akretion/docky@fix-py3-wheel-tag
